.SS "template<typename \fBT\fP , \fBqualifier\fP Q> \fBGLM_FUNC_DISCARD_DECL\fP \fBvoid\fP glm::sortEigenvalues (\fBvec\fP< 4, \fBT\fP, \fBQ\fP > & eigenvalues, \fBmat\fP< 4, 4, \fBT\fP, \fBQ\fP > & eigenvectors)"
Assuming the provided covariance matrix \fRcovarMat\fP is symmetric and real-valued, this function find the \fRD\fP Eigenvalues of the matrix, and also provides the corresponding Eigenvectors\&. Note: the data in \fRoutEigenvalues\fP and \fRoutEigenvectors\fP are in matching order, i\&.e\&. \fRoutEigenvector[i]\fP is the Eigenvector of the Eigenvalue \fRoutEigenvalue[i]\fP\&. This is a numeric implementation to find the Eigenvalues, using 'QL decomposition` (variant of QR decomposition: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/QR_decomposition)\&. / /
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcovarMat\fP A symmetric, real-valued covariance matrix, e\&.g\&. computed from computeCovarianceMatrix /
.br
\fIoutEigenvalues\fP Vector to receive the found eigenvalues /
.br
\fIoutEigenvectors\fP Matrix to receive the found eigenvectors corresponding to the found eigenvalues, as column vectors / 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
